 ## Ranked
 
+MyAI Office 0.7.3 narrows DOCX TOC result fidelity: complex HYPERLINK fields retain real tabs,
+formatted runs and nested page references instead of flattening them into atomic text. Synthetic
+round-trip checks and private native/WPS comparisons cover the dotted-leader failure. The private
+document still places its TOC across a page boundary; Chinese font metrics and pagination remain
+unresolved, and no forced page breaks or global spacing changes are introduced.
+Release-font validation also exposed an ignored East Asian alias in mixed-script runs; recognized
+aliases now select their available substitute. This does not make substitutes metric-identical.
+
+MyAI Office 0.6.1 narrows the legacy DOC compatibility gap: external paragraph/table properties, separate row terminators, fixed grids, shading, cell borders and CJK font defaults are now read. One private two-page document and synthetic regression cases were checked; this does not close the general pagination or corpus-validation gaps.
+
+MyAI Office 0.7.2 further covers nested TOC cached paragraphs, per-row column boundaries and
+full-width cells, empty-cell formatting, paragraph grid opt-outs, and text-box internal margins.
+Private copies are opened in installed WPS for reference and rendered natively by MyAI; no WPS
+code/assets or external Office engine is embedded. Remaining differences in pagination, floating
+objects and cached TOC page numbers still require document-by-document validation.
+Experimental section-grid/layout changes were withheld because they introduced a table-row
+pagination regression in one private file. The grid gap is not closed by this release.
